SinglePointConstrList;1;123456;1;4;12;17;22;26;27;30;32;34;51;53;55;67;72;77;81;82;83;84;85;86;87;88;89
SinglePointConstrList;1;123456;99;Through;106
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Euler mesh
# 10 x 10 x 10 hexahedra over a 120 mm cube; the x planes are biased (finer
# in the middle) by BIAS 1
EulerMeshGenerator;1;Box;;;;;;;-60.;-60.;-60.;120.;120.;120.;10;10;10;;;;Euler;10;;;;;;Center;1.;1.;1.;1
EulerMeshBias;1;-60.;0.5;3;;;-20.;;4;;;20.;2.;3
EulerRegionProp;10;Hydrodynamic;20
# Air
EulerMat;11;1.2E-12;1
GammaLawStateEquation;1;1.4;2.87E+8
# Gravity on the gas (9810 mm/s2 along -Z)
EulerBodyForce;1;;9810.;;0.;0.;-1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- initial gas
# Four regions (the highest level wins): ambient air everywhere, a denser
# cylinder, the gas inside the small closed surface, a hot sphere
EulerInitialRegions;20;21
InitialConditionRegion;1;21;Sphere;31;11;41;0.
InitialConditionRegion;2;21;Cylinder;32;11;42;1.
InitialConditionRegion;3;21;Surface;33;11;43;2.
InitialConditionRegion;4;21;Sphere;34;11;44;3.
SphereShape;31;0.;0.;0.;200.
CylinderShape;32;-30.;-30.;-45.;-30.;-30.;45.;10.
InitialSurfaceVolume;33;301;Inside;On;On
ContactElemSurface;301;2001;Through;2006
SphereShape;34;0.;0.;10.;15.
InitialConditionValues;41;;Density;1.2E-12;SpecificInternalEnergy;2.083E+11
InitialConditionValues;42;;Density;2.4E-12;SpecificInternalEnergy;2.083E+11
InitialConditionValues;43;;Density;1.8E-12;SpecificInternalEnergy;2.083E+11
InitialConditionValues;44;;Density;1.2E-11;SpecificInternalEnergy;1.E+12
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- coupling
# The whole box (BCPROP 101) couples the gas inside to the shells
ContactPropertyRegion;101;1
EulerLagrangeCoupling;1;101;Outside;On;On;1;1;Standard;;;;;;;;;;;;;1
# The Eulerian pressure acts in full on the whole surface (interaction factor
# 1); the ambient pressure of 0.1 MPa acts from the covered side (PLCOVER on
# the continuation line)
CouplingOptions;1;1;0;Constant;1.;Constant;0.1
# The subsurfaces: a vent hole (top), a permeable side (+Y), an outflow
# element (+X), a time-dependent inflow element (-X), a cohesive bottom
ContactElemSurface;201;1506
ContactElemSurface;202;1301;Through;1316
ContactElemSurface;203;1106
ContactElemSurface;204;1006
ContactElemSurface;205;1401;Through;1416
GasBagLeakage;1;1;201;GasBagVentHole;1;Constant;1.
GasBagLeakage;2;1;202;SurfacePermeability;2;Constant;0.5
GasBagLeakage;3;1;203;PorousFlowBoundary;3
GasBagLeakage;4;1;204;PorousTimeFlowBoundary;4;Table;51
GasBagVentHole;1;Small;Both;0.1;1.2E-12;2.083E+11
SurfacePermeability;2;1.E+3;;Out;0.1;1.2E-12;2.083E+11
PorousFlowBoundary;3;FlowDirection;Out;Method;VelocityQuantity
PorousTimeFlowBoundary;4;In;Table;52
# The area of the inflow element opens over 0.2 ms; its inflow velocity
TableDynamic1;51;;;0.;0.;2.E-4;1.;1.;1.;EndTable
TableDynamic1;52;;;0.;0.;2.E-4;5.E+3;1.;5.E+3;EndTable
# Cohesive friction on the bottom (tension up to 0.05 MPa)
CouplingCohesiveFriction;1;1;205;1
CohesiveFriction;1;0.05;0.01;1.E+3
